      "message": "Here are more details to justify the wait-and-retry would work for some cases.\n\nIn [af_bluetooth.c](https://source.corp.google.com/h/chromium/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/kernel/v5.10/net/bluetooth/af_bluetooth.c;l\u003d1?q\u003daf_bluetooth.c\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fchromium%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain:src%2Fthird_party%2Fkernel%2Fv5.10%2Fnet%2Fbluetooth%2F)::bt_init, there is a tiny window that PH_BLUETOOTH is registered but mgmt is not initialized. This causes the BtSocket::open to succeed but BtSocket::bind to fail. In this case, a short wait and retry should work.",
